---
id: org.dxos.plugin.finance
name: FinancePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Finance research over public sources that need no API key. Every source follows one shape:
**external source → ECHO feed → extract**. An ingest reads a source and appends its items to an
ECHO `Feed` of their own, each carrying a foreign key to its origin (`Obj.Meta.keys`, e.g.
`{ source: 'sec.gov', id: <accession> }`, `{ source: 'news.google.com', id: <guid> }`), deduped on
that key so reruns are idempotent. Extraction reads the feeds, never the network, and writes one
RDF fact store, recording each item's foreign key as the provenance of its facts.

Text items — news headlines, press releases, central-bank and statistics releases, Reddit posts,
crypto news — are magazine `Subscription.Post` objects (the plugin reuses plugin-magazine's feed
parsing and post type) and go through LLM extraction with a finance vocabulary pack, a ticker
mention index, sentiment and event classification. Structured rows — daily prices, FINRA short
volume, SEC Form 4 insider trades, 13F holdings, company filings, House disclosure filings — are
`Observation` objects and become facts deterministically, with no model calls, on the same
predicates and the same company entities, so one query joins a company's news sentiment with its
prices and insider trades.

The plugin itself is headless and contributes the types; the pipeline runs as the opt-in
`plugin-finance:run` moon task against a local, persistent client.

## Dependencies

```mdl
uses org.dxos.spec.changelog: The dialect of this spec's `## Changelog` and its attribution rules.
uses org.dxos.plugin.magazine: Feed parsing (`FeedParser`) and the `Subscription.Post` text item type.
```

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`     |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0` |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

### Types registered by this plugin

| Type                  | Source                               |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `Feed.Feed`           | `@dxos/echo`                         |
| `Finance.Observation` | this plugin                          |
| `Subscription.Post`   | `@dxos/plugin-magazine/Subscription` |

### Sources

| Feed                 | Source                                                                  | Item          | Extraction    |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------- |
| `news`               | Google News search (weekly windows, per ticker), Yahoo per ticker, CNBC, MarketWatch, Nasdaq, Seeking Alpha | `Post`        | LLM           |
| `press-releases`     | PR Newswire                                                             | `Post`        | LLM           |
| `central-banks`      | Federal Reserve press and speeches, ECB, Bank of England, BEA           | `Post`        | LLM           |
| `reddit`             | r/investing, r/stocks, r/SecurityAnalysis, r/wallstreetbets             | `Post`        | LLM           |
| `crypto`             | CoinDesk, The Block                                                     | `Post`        | LLM           |
| `sec-filings`        | EDGAR company feeds: 8-K, 10-Q, 10-K, S-1                               | `Observation` | deterministic |
| `sec-insider-trades` | EDGAR Form 4 XML                                                        | `Observation` | deterministic |
| `sec-13f`            | EDGAR 13F information tables of a few well-known filers                 | `Observation` | deterministic |
| `prices`             | Yahoo Finance chart endpoint, daily bars                                | `Observation` | deterministic |
| `finra-short-volume` | FINRA daily short-sale volume files                                     | `Observation` | deterministic |
| `house-disclosures`  | House Clerk financial-disclosure index (periodic transaction reports)   | `Observation` | deterministic |

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Ingest into ECHO feeds

  req F-1.1: Each source writes its items to an ECHO feed of its own, of kind
    `org.dxos.plugin.finance.feed/<feed>`.

  req F-1.2: Every item carries one foreign key to its origin, and an ingest appends only items
    whose key the feed does not hold, so a rerun adds only what is new. A text item is also a
    duplicate of a stored item with the same outlet and normalized headline.

  req F-1.3: A source that fails is reported and skipped; the others still run. Sources that need
    an API key are not used.

  req F-1.4: Requests are polite: SEC EDGAR under its 10 requests a second with a user agent that
    names the tool and the DXOS project contact, Reddit with a descriptive user agent and a pause
    between requests.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: One fact store

  req F-2.1: Extraction reads the ECHO feeds, never the network, and writes one RDF fact store.

  req F-2.2: Every fact's `attribution.source` is its item's foreign key, `<source>:<id>`.

  req F-2.3: Text items go through `indexFactsBatch` with the seed ontology, schema.org and the
    finance packs, and the listed companies as known entities; then the ticker mention index
    (regex, then model linking for names), sentiment per article and per ticker, and event types.
    Each model stage is attributed to its own `AiUsage` stage.

  req F-2.4: Structured rows become facts without a model, on predicates of the finance
    namespace, about the same company IRIs the text facts use.

  req F-2.5: Extraction resumes: an item whose content hash matches its cursor is skipped.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: The plugin

  req F-3.1: The plugin is headless and contributes a schema module registering the types in the
    table above.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: A rerun adds nothing new
  given: A source has been ingested.
  when: It is ingested again with the same upstream items.
  then: No item is appended, and the feed holds each foreign key once.
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: One ticker across sources
  given: The pipeline has run over news, prices and Form 4.
  when: `plugin-finance:query` runs for a ticker.
  then: Each day shows the ticker's news sentiment, close, daily return, short-volume ratio and
    insider trades, all read from the one fact store.
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `org.dxos.spec.changelog` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: Finance extraction lives in a new plugin, plugin-finance, which imports feed parsing and the post type from plugin-magazine instead of duplicating them.
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-3.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Every source runs external source → ECHO feed → extract, each item keyed by its origin, and extraction records that key as the facts' provenance.
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: One fact store holds text and structured facts; structured rows become facts without a model on the same predicates and company entities.
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.3, F-2.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Text items are magazine `Subscription.Post` objects and structured rows are one `Finance.Observation` type with a `kind`, numeric `values` and text `labels`. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-3.1]
  why: A post already models a feed item and the magazine UI can show it; one observation type keeps the six structured sources to one schema the deterministic extractor switches on.
  rejected: A type per structured source, which multiplies schemas for rows that differ only in their fields.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Daily prices come from Yahoo Finance's keyless chart endpoint; Stooq is dropped. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3]
  why: Stooq's CSV now answers with a JavaScript proof-of-work challenge, which a tool must not bypass.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Dropped sources that refused keyless access when checked: StockTwits (403 behind Cloudflare), GlobeNewswire (403), Business Wire (empty feed), BLS (403), Yahoo's rssindex (404), Investing.com (timeout), Senate eFD (needs a session and an agreement form). House disclosures are read as filing records only, since their trades are in PDFs. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-7: SEC EDGAR is read with the user agent `dxos-finance-research contact@dxos.org`, the DXOS project's public contact that plugin-ibkr's EDGAR client already sends. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: EDGAR answers 403 to a user agent without a contact address, and no person's address may be used.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Text extraction runs without thinking. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-16
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.3]
  why: On a 150-headline sample it found 0.97 facts per item against 0.71 with thinking, 93% on finance terms, at half the cost.
```
